AB  - Predicting next failure of the filler's differential pressure of heating ventilating and air conditioning (HVAC) system provides for a higher performance of the system. There exist various fluctuating parameters that contribute in this paramount prediction. In the current study, the traditional method of linear regression and artificial neural network are applied as means of prediction, and it is shown that the performance is improved shen supplemented with a decision tree approach. The outcome reveals which one can more effectively predict trends and behavioral patterns as well as maintenance requirement of such systems with limited considered attributes. Hence, the empirical data is retrieved and a new method for predictive maintenance illustrated using HVAC system of Ecole de technologie superieure (ETS). (C) 2015, IFAC (International Federation of Automatic Control) Hosting by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
