AB  - In today's living environment the availability of cooled goods such as fresh fruit, vegetables, meat and even refrigerated groceries is indispensable. This is the reason why cooling is becoming more and more important for automatic control. One important factor is overtemperature disturbance in the industrial food refrigeration process because it can lead to health risks for customers and also a great economic damage for the operator. Find a solution for this issue we can use predictive maintenance models. The first step described in this paper is to implement and present an algorithm that classifies relevant cooling positions in selected industrial refrigeration facilities with regard to their periodic overtemperature disturbance behavior. On the basis of the results, three predictive models for premature disturbance detection: Logistic Regression, Decision Trees, and Random Forest are developed. The three models are compared to each other and the validity of the proposed method is demonstrated by means of a numerical example.
