AB  - Residential energy consumption has surpassed the commercial sector, emphasizing the growing need for more efficient HVAC systems. This study focuses on developing predictive models to estimate the power consumption of split system heat pumps, in residential applications. Leveraging real-time data inputs and advanced computational techniques, the research compares multiple models, including multiple linear regression, artificial neural networks, fine tree decision models, and Gaussian process regression. Empirical data collected from residential split system heat pumps were used to predict compressor power consumption, with the fine tree model demonstrating the highest accuracy across error indices. These predictive models are vital for optimizing HVAC system efficiency, reducing energy consumption, and minimizing costs. By simulating system performance, they facilitate informed adjustments, and predictive maintenance, and ensure compliance with energy regulations, making sure that HVAC systems remain reliable, cost-effective, and environmentally sustainable.
