AB  - The integration of Additive Manufacturing (AM) and the Internet of Things (IoT) is transforming industries by facilitating real-time data monitoring, automation, and predictive maintenance. Understanding user perspectives on AM-IoT adoption is essential for accelerating its implementation. This study combines statistical analysis and deep learning-based predictive modeling to analyze survey responses from healthcare professionals, AM specialists, IoT experts, researchers, and other stakeholders. A structured 23-question survey was conducted, covering awareness, benefits, challenges, and future adoption trends. Statistical analysis using the Statistical Package for Social Sciences (SPSS) platform confirmed data reliability, with a mean score of 3.8 indicating a positive inclination toward AM-IoT, a standard deviation of 1.1 reflecting moderate variability, and Cronbach's Alpha of 0.78 ensuring internal consistency. An Artificial Neural Network (ANN) model achieved 85% accuracy in classifying user perspectives, while a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) model predicted adoption trends from 2024 to 2030. Results indicate that researchers have the highest adoption rates, followed by IoT and AM professionals, whose adoption levels converge by 2030. The LSTM model achieved an R-2 value of 78%, confirming strong predictive accuracy. These findings highlight the importance of awareness, cost reduction, and real-time monitoring in driving adoption, providing valuable insights for policymakers, researchers, and industry leaders.
