AB  - Addressing the challenges in predicting the lifespan of industrial relays, this study proposes a fusion prediction method based on Physics-Informed Neural Network (PINN). Through statistical correlation analysis of key electrical parameters of relays (pickup voltage, release voltage, pickup time, release time, coil resistance) against lifecycle, a significant positive correlation was identified between the voltage margin ratio and lifespan. Building upon this insight, the established PINN model innovatively integrates physical mechanisms to form a physics-consistent loss function. Validation using the C9-A41X/DC24VR relay dataset demonstrates that the model achieves near-perfect predictive accuracy (R-2=0.9999). This research opens up new technical pathways for reliability assessment and predictive maintenance of industrial relays.
