KW  - Deep Learning
KW  - Predictive Maintenance
KW  - PROGNOSTICS
AB  - Molecular pumps are critical components in the Experimental Advanced Superconducting Tokamak facility, and accurately predicting their Remaining Useful Life is essential for optimizing maintenance planning and experiment scheduling. However, precise Remaining Useful Life prediction remains challenging due to the complex operating environment and inherent data noise. To enhance prediction accuracy and model robustness, this study proposes an innovative C-Transformer hybrid model. This novel approach combines the local feature extraction capabilities of Convolution Neural Networks with the global dependency capturing abilities of Transformers, rendering it more effective in processing time series data. Using molecular pump fault data for verification demonstrated the superior performance of the proposed method in predicting the remaining service life, achieving root mean square error (RMSE) and mean absolute error (MAE) scores of 583 seconds and 501 seconds, respectively. These results significantly outperform other comparative methods. This approach not only provides a reliable Remaining Useful Life prediction solution for molecular pumps in the Experimental Advanced Superconducting Tokamak facility's vacuum system but also offers valuable insights for developing predictive maintenance strategies in other complex industrial systems. By implementing this method, it is possible to prevent irreversible damage caused by prolonged overload operation, reduce maintenance costs, and enhance overall operational efficiency and reliability.
