AB  - The operational state of lithium battery wafer roll pressing equipment critically impacts battery manufacturing, with electrode thickness consistency directly linked to equipment status. Existing predictive maintenance methods for such equipment often suffer from low accuracy, hindering effective performance degradation prediction. To address this, this paper proposes a novel hybrid CNN-BiGRU model integrating a self-attention (SA) mechanism for predicting the RUL of lithium battery pole piece double-roll pressing equipment. Our method leverages CNN for spatial feature extraction from vibration signals and BiGRU for capturing temporal dependencies. Crucially, the innovative SA mechanism enables the model to adaptively identify and focus on the most diagnostically valuable time-frequency features, improving the model's sensitivity to early degradation patterns. Experimental validation with real industrial data demonstrates that the CNN-BiGRU-SA model achieves superior RUL prediction accuracy, thereby providing a robust tool for predictive maintenance that can substantially reduce unplanned downtime and improve production efficiency in battery manufacturing facilities.
