AB  - An innovative solution for predictive maintenance in IIoT systems combining quantum computing with the proficiency of LSTM neural networks is proposed by us. Our concept is guided by a hybrid quantum-classical architecture to facilitate quantum computing to exploit highdimensional industrial sensor measurements while preserving crucial temporal relationships through particular quantum channels. Through the combination of the representational ingenuity of quantum circuits, along with the sequence-based modelling of classical LSTMs, QE-LSTM is uniquely positioned to handle complicated time series coming out of industrial sensors. At the heart of our methodology are the following unique elements: center dot A collaborative framework integrating quantum and classical technologies allowing for the quantum computer to manage the complex analysis of high dimensional sensor data in the industry. center dot Quantum channel designs were aimed at minimizing temporal dependencies in temporal series industrial measurements, thereby maximizing the quality of sequential analysis. center dot Under ODS hindcasting, QE-LSTM improved F1 by 4-5 percentage points on SECOM and reduced RMSE and NASA Score on C-MAPSS; trends were consistent on IMMD (Tables 1-2). In the application of failure detection of bearing, QE-LSTM improves F1 over classical baselines on SECOM by 4-5 pp, with similar gains on IMMD; results on C-MAPSS (RUL) show consistent reductions in RMSE and NASA score.
