AB  - Smart buildings play a vital role in modern urban development, with Internet of Things (IoT) integration transforming facility management and user experience. However, these systems also introduce significant cyber security risks. This research explored how Artificial Intelligence (AI) can address these threats by applying Machine Learning (ML) and predictive analytics to detect and prevent cyber attacks.
   By analyzing network behavior, attack patterns, and vulnerabilities, a proactive AI-driven model developed and deployed to enhance threat detection and automate responses. The TON IoT dataset is used to train and validate the intrusion detection model to improve the accuracy, and strengthen security strategies tailored for smart infrastructure and sensitive data protection. A number of ML models are applied on collected datasets and found that XGBoost consistently outperformed others in accuracy, recall, and AUC.
