AB  - Lack of sufficient experience and easy access to previous historical and technical information on maintenance operations, along with various changes in maintenance staff, increase cost and decrease life cycle of building facilities. This study addresses this problem by presenting a framework to (1) use historical experience for a location-aware maintenance solution recommendation and (2) improve access to building facilities' technical and historical information on-site. For this purpose, the framework integrates three digital technologies: Augmented Reality (AR), Building Information Model (BIM), and Artificial Intelligence (AI). The framework enables communication with facility managers and staff by natural language with the aid of the AI module. This module also employs case-based reasoning to recommend appropriate solutions using previous successful maintenance operations. The BIM module includes facility information and its maintenance history. The AR module recognizes elements on-site with electronic mobile devices and represents information about facilities. A University building case study is employed to evaluate the practicality and effectiveness of the proposed framework. Facility managers and staff of this building used the implemented framework and indicated that this framework is easy to use and suggests appropriate maintenance solutions.
