AB  - The growing adoption of image-guided unmanned aerial vehicles (UAVs) in building inspection and maintenance has increased the demand for high-quality datasets to support computer vision models. However, there is a lack of labeled image databases focused on modern architectural features, particularly glass facades and windows. This paper presents a curated dataset composed of selected images of contemporary building facades, preprocessed and manually annotated to support classification tasks using deep learning. The dataset includes 3805 image samples, labeled and annotated for key components such as windows, doors, and structural elements. Data were collected via targeted web searches, screened for relevance and quality, annotated in YOLO format, and validated for consistency. This work addresses a critical gap in publicly available resources and supports the development of AI-based UAV systems for tele-operated and autonomous maintenance. It also enables real-time visual analysis in cyber-physical and Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) applications related to urban monitoring. Copyright (C) 2025 The Authors. This is an open access article under the CC BY-NC-ND license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/)
