AB  - This paper proposes an analytical model to assess the specific impact of a complete demagnetization fault affecting two adjacent permanent-magnets, influencing various parameters of an external rotor permanent-magnet synchronous motor. This work aims to provide a comprehensive assessment of the machine's condition, identify failure levels, and offer valuable information for diagnosis, monitoring, and predictive maintenance through the identification of sensitive harmonics. The model is further validated by 2D finite element simulations and by analysis based on experimental results under healthy and faulty conditions. It validates and demonstrates the effectiveness of the proposed approach to fault detection and diagnosis, thus providing a solid basis for potential implementation in the industrial application. The proposed analytical model significantly reduces computation time while maintaining adequate accuracy, and so facilitating magnet fault simulation.
