TI  - A hybrid prognostic approach combined with deep Bayesian transformer and enhanced particle filter for remaining useful life prediction of bearings
T2  - MEASUREMENT
LA  - English
KW  - Lifetime prognostics
KW  - Rolling bearing
KW  - Feature fusion
KW  - Bayesian Transformer
KW  - Particle filter
AB  - As critical components of mechanical equipment, bearings are vital to ensuring reliability and safety. Accurate remaining useful life (RUL) prediction is essential for timely maintenance, failure prevention, and cost reduction. This paper proposes a hybrid bearing life prediction method integrating a Bayesian Transformer with enhanced Particle Filtering. First, an improved prognostic minimum redundancy maximum relevance (mRMR) feature selection method is developed to identify optimal health indicators (HIs), leveraging an autoencoder to generate HIs and capture diverse feature representations. Next, the HIs are fed into a deep Bayesian Transformer for onestep-ahead prediction, yielding RUL estimates with quantified uncertainty. Finally, the inferred bearing state serves as a virtual measurement, and a Switching Improved Pearson Particle Filter (SIPPF) enables closed-loop state estimation, facilitating RUL prediction and its probability density function (PDF). The proposed method is validated on multiple datasets, demonstrating its effectiveness in predictive maintenance for mechanical systems.
