TI  - Scenario-Adaptive Building Defect Inspection by Active Learning
T2  - COMPUTING IN CIVIL ENGINEERING 2024: ARTIFICIAL INTELLIGENCE, AUTOMATION AND ROBOTICS, AND HUMAN-CENTERED INNOVATIONS
LA  - English
CP  - 2024 International Conference on Computing in Civil Engineering-I3CE
AB  - Computer Vision (CV) and Deep Learning (DL) have emerged as prevalent technologies in building defect inspection during construction and maintenance under diverse and dynamic scenarios. However, existing CV-based DL models are majorly developed and implemented in certain building environments for detecting or segmenting distinct defect classes. These specialized approaches limit their robustness and adaptability to new and more complex scenarios, encountering challenges, including (1) the instability in DL model performance caused by the variability in feature distribution across feature-determined training scenarios and feature-changing test scenarios; and (2) the significant cost and time required for annotating a comprehensive training data set. To address these issues, this paper proposes a novel DL workflow integrating Active Learning (AL). AL strategically selects the most informative unlabeled features to improve the computational efficiency of training. The successful implementation of the proposed DL model holds promise for more effective and efficient AI-aided building inspection processes, characterized by continuous learning and adaptability to diverse scenarios.
